{"w":2400,"h":2857,"lines":[{"y":0.06523193954131723,"w":0.052040767669677732,"c":1,"h":0.014884958073674182,"t":"Test 4","x":0.081246052071245037},{"t":"Questions 24-26","h":0.014695591322603119,"x":0.083044983691445445,"y":0.11336599033407169,"w":0.15224913279215493,"c":1},{"x":0.083044982856099708,"y":0.14970930234982505,"h":0.018940102728702835,"c":1,"t":"Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.","w":0.32698961893717449},{"t":"Write the correct letter in boxes 24-26 on your answer sheet.","x":0.082964905536990541,"h":0.020717666898264264,"w":0.50706171671549483,"c":1,"y":0.18439686577343939},{"x":0.081231320643655583,"t":"24 What point does the writer make about primary schools in India in the sixth","y":0.21942217046781187,"w":0.66452992757161466,"c":1,"h":0.020919024318644341},{"h":0.016047901503267292,"w":0.097884267171223949,"t":"paragraph?","x":0.12071911716476208,"c":1,"y":0.24274238283046357},{"x":0.11937716124528755,"t":"<","y":0.26744185937303067,"w":0.020761248270670579,"h":0.017441862358589799,"c":1},{"x":0.16248114100103161,"h":0.022033262953548016,"c":1,"y":0.26545165143108351,"t":"Exposure to English outside of school is of limited benefit.","w":0.48293426513671878},{"x":0.16252529785860087,"c":1,"y":0.28478656830721794,"t":"Children learn English more easily when they are well motivated.","h":0.021070082593080963,"w":0.53651046752929688},{"y":0.3032192667452851,"t":"Poor children may be disadvantaged further by being instructed in English.","w":0.62301783243815101,"h":0.021019506487836459,"c":1,"x":0.16252624274337393},{"c":1,"w":0.67834630330403645,"x":0.12275493424369993,"t":"D There is little consistency across schools with regard to instruction in English.","y":0.32112120138933586,"h":0.021840371144577042},{"c":1,"y":0.3561587287719139,"t":"25 What is Tsimpli suggesting when she uses the phrase 'that ship has sailed'?","w":0.66120880126953119,"h":0.023766434217683763,"x":0.082909836122700586},{"t":"A The findings of the report may be of little help to some Indian schoolchildren.","x":0.1227213185295408,"y":0.38491439831612551,"h":0.022369474193447592,"w":0.68358627319335941,"c":1},{"w":0.65934397379557286,"t":"Instruction in English could be better adapted to the needs of schoolchildren.","h":0.022418804982894724,"c":1,"x":0.14869517755779432,"y":0.40310144760067135},{"y":0.42732558142607258,"h":0.01308139510051276,"w":0.015570934613545723,"c":1,"t":"C","x":0.12283736997696418},{"t":"D","w":0.015570934613545737,"y":0.44476744217390873,"x":0.12283736999138169,"h":0.014534882851794828,"c":1},{"y":0.42273587414180214,"c":1,"h":0.020951763577524596,"x":0.15910828095438603,"t":"Schools have had limited success in teaching English as a separate subject.","w":0.6247011311848959},{"y":0.43933248448309981,"t":"It is too late to remove English completely as a language of instruction in","x":0.16078581581342197,"w":0.60754079182942711,"h":0.024438151952851705,"c":1},{"h":0.018502332181510095,"c":1,"t":"schools.","y":0.46109992324440241,"x":0.16236610611375957,"w":0.071649246215820306},{"w":0.61271550496419269,"t":"26 In the eighth paragraph, what do we learn has surprised researchers?","h":0.022290109670437541,"c":1,"x":0.084645172817916142,"y":0.49533750688382705},{"h":0.021488407260475628,"w":0.56419031778971351,"x":0.16256782090676902,"c":1,"t":"Boys and girls from low socio-economic groups have similar general","y":0.52397492774794885},{"t":"intelligence levels.","x":0.16262975687785253,"h":0.017573071660655137,"c":1,"y":0.54505813924189228,"w":0.157439448038737},{"w":0.6213900248209635,"h":0.023361566435464831,"t":"The age at which children move into a slum does not affect their academic","y":0.55866256590297192,"c":1,"x":0.16076679822741749},{"t":"pertormance.","h":0.016259882815489735,"w":0.11424036661783854,"x":0.16433310339766949,"c":1,"y":0.582713081715999},{"h":0.013081395100512871,"c":1,"y":0.60174418606166213,"x":0.12456747442117534,"t":"C","w":0.013840829531351725},{"w":0.62994420369466142,"c":1,"x":0.16255010692623234,"y":0.59682931226737346,"t":"Slum children and children from other urban poor backgrounds have similar","h":0.02202168472001742},{"y":0.61918604657106069,"t":"life experiences.","x":0.16435986127807833,"w":0.1384083048502604,"h":0.015988371937820545,"c":1},{"y":0.63808139534218544,"c":1,"w":0.013840829531351712,"h":0.013081395100512871,"t":"D","x":0.12629757821010271},{"x":0.16420182453182766,"w":0.63013432820638027,"h":0.024207643064441453,"c":1,"t":"The literacy and numeracy skills of slum children are not lower than those of","y":0.63189621851480049},{"t":"children from other urban poor backgrounds.","x":0.1642792299445881,"y":0.65395641402912308,"h":0.018925312434651009,"c":1,"w":0.37903472900390622},{"t":"88","y":0.96366279075642969,"w":0.024221453666687029,"x":0.086505190035168614,"h":0.01308139510051276,"c":1},{"h":0.017496786391176244,"t":"→ • p. 124","x":0.11937716365074517,"y":0.96220930202725796,"c":1,"w":0.13494809468587238}]}